   {"on": "using the hypotheses not as first principles, but only as hypotheses", "text": "Plato's criticism of the geometers. They take their starting points on trust. A philosopher should ask why those starting points are true. Two thousand years later, mathematicians did exactly that, with surprising results, as the lecture explains."},
   {"on": "the habit which is concerned with geometry and the cognate sciences I suppose that you would term understanding and not reason", "text": "Plato ranks geometry high, above opinion and belief, but just below the highest knowledge. It is a training for the mind on its way to the Good."}
